  "ingredients": [
    "4 cups water",
    "1 teaspoon fine salt",
    "1 cup polenta",
    "3 tablespoons butter, divided",
    "0.5 cup freshly grated Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese, plus more for garnish"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/kTD3y9zoylxZuZ455QBcdNPVVUg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-234933-how-to-make-perfect-polenta-ddmfs-step1-3x4-2d4e759f4b3f4a5a804a2cff10c56f85.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/234933/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring water and salt to a boil in a large saucepan; pour polenta slowly into boiling water, whisking constantly until there are no lumps.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/gWLi5SEP_H7LmIetYVhlMzk0P6k=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-234933-how-to-make-perfect-polenta-ddmfs-step2-3x4-9c2f1d6a5f7e40839667a3d0606c00c3.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/234933/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduce heat to low and simmer, whisking often, until polenta starts to thicken, about 5 minutes. Polenta mixture should still be slightly loose. Cover and cook for 30 minutes, whisking every 5 to 6 minutes. When polenta is too thick to whisk, stir with a wooden spoon. Polenta is done when texture is creamy and the individual grains are tender. Cooking time will depend on the polenta grind.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/gyG5c59mRA4BSI4vt3Ys9LnGpAY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-234933-how-to-make-perfect-polenta-ddmfs-step3-1-3x4-3961974ba0994691b448222d4ca57551.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/234933/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn off heat and gently stir 2 tablespoons butter into polenta until butter partially melts; mix 1/2 cup Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese into polenta until cheese has melted. Cover and let stand for 5 minutes to thicken.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Yp_f_HwLN0V3nACeLcjNtFP5cRo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-234933-how-to-make-perfect-polenta-ddmfs-step4-3x4-0d1ec69ad15246f1a9e58d38bf1b534b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/234933/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir polenta and transfer to a serving bowl. Top polenta with remaining 1 tablespoon butter and about 1 tablespoon freshly grated Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese for garnish.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ihBVI29B6Kz6ErONdDWTfDR6LCg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-RM-234933-how-to-make-perfect-polenta-ddmfs-3x4-5d4dc27b993a4c4bb33db0e1163dbbba.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/234933/step_05.webp"
    }
  ],
